PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
The panel maintains unanimous consensus on Choice A (Duloxetine + Gabapentin) for managing fibromyalgia with prominent affective, neuropathic, and sleep-related symptoms. Duloxetine targets the central pain pathways, major depression, and generalized anxiety, while gabapentin treats comorbid restless legs syndrome and paresthesias and improves sleep architecture. Potential concerns regarding antidepressant-induced restless legs exacerbation and NSAID bleeding risks are clinically manageable, whereas alternative monotherapies and regimens fail to cover both clinical domains.
}

